          %h2#basic_definitions Basic definitions
          %h3#in_terms_of_looping_by_representation_spheres In terms of looping by representation spheres
          %p
            The definition of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectrum"} G-spectrum
            is typically given in generalization of the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate-free+spectrum"} coordinate-free spectrum
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-universe"} G-universe
            in this context is (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay"} Greenlees-May, p. 10
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            equipped with a linear
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            that is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable"} countably
            many copies of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of (finite dimensional? -DMR)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            contains at least a copy of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\infty
          %p
            Each such subspace of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            (representation contained in
            = succeed "?" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %em indexing space
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"}> RO(G)-grading
            ). For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subset W
            indexing spaces, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo −
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W-V
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+complement"} orthogonal complement
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^V
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any (pointed)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^V := [S^V,X]
            for the corresponding (based) sphere space.
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"} G-space
            in the following means a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            equipped with a continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            that fixes the base point. A morphism of
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-equivariant." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            A weak equivalence of
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-fixed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              \-spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (indexed on the chosen universe
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each indexing space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subset U
                a
                = succeed "-space" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E V
            %li
              %p
                for each pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subset W
                of indexing spaces a
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mi V
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo −
                          %mi V
                      %mi E
                      %mi W
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      E V \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Omega^{W-V} E W
                      \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : E \to E'
            of
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a morphism of
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_V : E V \to E' V
          %p
            This becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            by setting:
          %p
            a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %strong
              weak equivalence of
              = succeed "-spectra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            if for every indexing space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            the component
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_V
            is a weak equivalence of
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This may be expressed directly in terms of the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong
                homotopy group of a
                = succeed "-spectrum" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#in_terms_of_orthogonal_spectra_with_action
            In terms of orthogonal spectra with
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            … (
            %a{:href => "#Schwede15"}> Schwede 15
            )…
          %h3#in_terms_of_mackeyfunctors In terms of Mackey-functors
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functor"} Mackey functor
            with values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            (“spectral Mackey functor”) is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            on a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+correspondences"} (∞,1)-category of correspondences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Corr
                    %mn 1
                    %mi eff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_1^{eff}(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow Corr_1(\mathcal{C})
            which sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
