                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+McClure"} J.E. McClure
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
                %strong 1213
                (1986) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/equi.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0075778"} doi:10.1007/BFb0075778
            %li#tomDieck87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , Section II.6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups"} Transformation Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110858372"} doi:10.1515/9783110858372
          %p
            and a more modern version taking into account the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal categories of spectra
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant orthogonal spectra and S-modules
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0408/MMM.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0408/"} K-theory archive
          %p
            Solving the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arf-Kervaire+invariant+problem"} Arf-Kervaire invariant problem
            with methods of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            (and reviewing these):
          %ul
            %li#HillHopkinsRavenel09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"}> Michael Hill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"} Douglas Ravenel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the non-existence of elements of Kervaire invariant one
                %strong 184
                1 (2016)&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2016.184.1.1"}> doi:10.4007/annals.2016.184.1.1
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.3724"} arXiv:0908.3724
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/Skye_handout.pdf"} talk slides
            %li#HillHopkinsRavenel21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"}> Michael Hill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"} Douglas Ravenel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant Stable Homotopy Theory and the Kervaire Invariant Problem
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108917278"} doi:10.1017/9781108917278
          %p Lecture notes are in
          %ul
            %li#Blumberg17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Burnside category
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/a.debray/lecture_notes/m392c_EHT_notes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/adebray/equivariant_homotopy_theory"} GitHub
          %p Further introductions and surveys include the following
          %ul
            %li#Carlsson92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
                ,
                = succeed ",Topology," do
                  %em A survey of equivariant stable homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/carlsson1.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Bohmann
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anna+Marie+Bohmann"}> Anna Marie Bohmann
                ,
                %em Basic notions of equivariant stable homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://math.vanderbilt.edu/bohmanar/basicequivnotions.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#GreenleesMay
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} Equivariant stable homotopy theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+James"} Ioan James
                (ed.),
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                , pp. 279-325. 1995. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/Newthird.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"}> Brooke Shipley
                ,
                %em An introduction to equivariant homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://homepages.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/bonn.2.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/index.php?year=2016"} Talbot workshop 2016
          %p
            Lecture notes on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
            modeled as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            with
            = succeed "-actions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li#Schwede15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+Equivariant+Stable+Homotopy+Theory"} Lectures on Equivariant Stable Homotopy Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/schwede/equivariant.pdf"} pdf
          %p An alternative perspective on this is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+White"} David White
              %em An alternative approach to equivariant stable homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.3846"}> arXiv:1312.3846
              )
          %p
            Generalization from equivariance under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+groups"} compact topological groups
            (Hausdorff) and in particular to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+groups"} profinite groups
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-homotopy+theory"} pro-homotopy theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Fausk06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Halvard+Fausk"}> Halvard Fausk
              ,
              %em Equivariant homotopy theory for pro-spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609635"}> arXiv:math/0609635
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/May+recognition+theorem"} May recognition theorem
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spaces"} G-spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+G-spectra"} genuine G-spectra
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Costenoble and Warner,
              %em Fixed set systems of equivariant infinite loop spaces
              Transactions of the American mathematical society, volume 326, Number 2 (1991) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/pss/2001770"}> JSTOR
              )
          %p
            Characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
            %a{:href => "spectrum+object#ViaExcisiveFunctors"} via excisive functors
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spaces"} G-spaces
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              ,
              %em Continuous functors as a model for the equivariant stable homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0505512"}> arXiv:math.AT/0505512
              )
          %p
            The characterization of
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
            is discussed in example 3.4 (i) of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              %em Classification of stable model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Schwede-Shipley/class.final.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A construction of equivariant stable homotopy theory in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Mackey+functors"} spectral Mackey functors
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Guillou"}> Bert Guillou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                %em
                  Models of
                  = succeed "-spectra" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.3571"} arXiv:1110.3571
              %p
                %em
                  Permutative
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.3459"} arXiv:1207.3459
          %p
            see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Mackey+functor"} spectral Mackey functor
            for more references.
          %p
            A fully
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theoretic
            formulation:
          %ul
            %li#Barwick14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectral Mackey functors and equivariant algebraic K-theory (I)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1404.0108"} arXiv:1404.0108
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Glasman"} Saul Glasman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis+Nardin"} Denis Nardin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectral Mackey functors and equivariant algebraic K-theory (II)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.03098"} arxiv:1505.03098
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            characterizing equivariant stable homotopy theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Campion"}> Tim Campion
              ,
              %em Free duals and a new universal property for stable equivariant homotopy theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04207"}> arXiv:2302.04207
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on April 18, 2024 at 18:14:01.
